quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  25,12,"When it (i.e. the Fire of Hell) sees them from a distant place, they will hear it raging forcefully and roaring."
  25,13,"And when they are thrown into a narrow place inside it, bound together (in chains), they will pray for (their instant) annihilation."
  25,14,(They will be told:) ‘Do not pray today for a single annihilation but pray for many annihilations.’
  25,15,"Say: ‘Is that better, or the everlasting Paradise promised to the God-conscious, which will be their reward and destination?"
  25,16,"Therein, they will have whatever they wish, abiding forever. That is a promise from your Lord which will indeed be fulfilled.’"
  25,17,"On the Day when He shall gather them along with what they used to worship besides Allah, He will say: ‘Were it you (i.e. the false gods) who led these servants of Mine astray, or did they stray from the way (on their own)?’"
  25,18,They will say: ‘Glory be to You. It was not right for us to take any guardians besides You! But You made them and their fathers enjoy (the comforts of the world) until they forgot the Reminder. And they were a ruined people.’
  25,19,"(The idolators will be told:) ‘They (the false gods) have denied your claims. So you shall neither be able to avert (the punishment) nor find (any) help.’ And whoever among you commits wrong, We shall make him taste a terrible punishment."
  25,20,We never sent any messengers before you who did not eat food and walk in marketplaces. And We have made some of you a means of trial for others (to see) if you can be patient. And your Lord is All-Seeing.
